          answer: "Personal protective equipment selection for laboratory chemical handling in Oman must be matched to the specific chemical hazards \u2014 there is no single universal PPE standard. For general laboratory work, the minimum required is: chemical-resistant gloves (nitrile 4-mil or thicker for most solvents and dilute acids; butyl rubber or neoprene for concentrated acids, bases, and ketone solvents), safety goggles with splash guard (not safety spectacles \u2014 goggles seal against the face), a laboratory coat in cotton or FR-treated fabric (polyester melts and adheres to skin in fire), and closed-toe shoes. For higher-hazard work \u2014 concentrated corrosives, volatile toxic chemicals, carcinogenic substances \u2014 a face shield (worn over goggles, not instead of them), chemical-resistant apron, and half-face respirator with appropriate organic vapour or acid gas cartridges are added. Under Oman Ministry of Manpower OSH Decision 286/2008, employers must provide appropriate PPE free of charge and train workers on correct use and limitations. Global Chemicals LLC supplies PPE alongside laboratory chemicals for convenience."
